# Equinox Equity Ventures

Official website for **Equinox Equity Ventures** — a private equity firm deploying capital at the inflection point between cycles.

🌐 **Live site:** <https://your-username.github.io/equinox-equity-ventures>

-----

## Features

- Fully static — no framework, no build step required
- Single `index.html` with all CSS and JS inline
- External dependency: Google Fonts (Cormorant Garamond + Josefin Sans) via CDN
- Deploys automatically to GitHub Pages on every push to `main`

## Sections

|Section     |Description                                    |
|------------|-----------------------------------------------|
|Hero        |Animated moon phases, headline, CTA            |
|Stats       |Live count-up: AUM, portfolio count, IRR, years|
|About       |Orbital animation + firm narrative             |
|Philosophy  |Three investment pillars                       |
|Sector Focus|Interactive sector cards                       |
|Portfolio   |Tabbed view with detail modals                 |
|Team        |Partner bios via modal                         |
|Process     |Scroll-reveal timeline                         |
|Contact     |Form with validation and toast notification    |

## Deployment

### GitHub Pages (recommended)

1. Push this repo to GitHub
1. Go to **Settings → Pages**
1. Set source to **GitHub Actions**
1. The included workflow (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) handles the rest

Every push to `main` will automatically redeploy the site.

### Manual / Local

Just open `index.html` in any browser — no server needed.

```bash
open index.html        # macOS
start index.html       # Windows
xdg-open index.html    # Linux
```

## Customisation

All content is in `index.html`. Key areas to update:

- **Firm details** — name, AUM, IRR stats at the top of `<body>`
- **Portfolio companies** — search for `openPortModal(` calls
- **Team members** — search for `openTeamModal(` calls
- **Contact details** — search for `enquiries@equinoxequity.com`
- **Office locations** — search for `The Shard`
- **Colors** — CSS variables at the top of `<style>` (`:root` block)

